("v271", "type", "Sequence")
("v272", "type", "String")
("v272", "scalar", "What do I mean by God?")
("v271", "item", "v272")
("v270", "value", "v271")
("v252", "item", "v265")
("v273", "type", "Record")
("v273", "entry", "v274")
("v274", "type", "Entry")
("v274", "key", "tag")
("v275", "type", "String")
("v275", "scalar", "p")
("v274", "value", "v275")
("v273", "entry", "v276")
("v276", "type", "Entry")
("v276", "key", "attrs")
("v277", "type", "Record")
("v276", "value", "v277")
("v273", "entry", "v278")
("v278", "type", "Entry")
("v278", "key", "children")
("v279", "type", "Sequence")
("v280", "type", "String")
("v280", "scalar", "When I say God, I mean the source and sustainer of life, worthy of trust and worship because of goodness as well as power. The question is therefore moral as well as metaphysical: what kind of power deserves our love?")
("v279", "item", "v280")
("v278", "value", "v279")
("v252", "item", "v273")
("v281", "type", "Record")
("v281", "entry", "v282")
("v282", "type", "Entry")
("v282", "key", "tag")
("v283", "type", "String")
("v283", "scalar", "p")
("v282", "value", "v283")
("v281", "entry", "v284")
("v284", "type", "Entry")
("v284", "key", "attrs")
("v285", "type", "Record")
("v284", "value", "v285")
("v281", "entry", "v286")
("v286", "type", "Entry")
("v286", "key", "children")
("v287", "type", "Sequence")
("v288", "type", "String")
("v288", "scalar", "The kenotic account developed here understands divine power through self-giving love. Kenosis means self-emptying: using power in a way that makes room for another person’s life and agency. In this reading, love can restrain power and can also require protection, judgment or intervention. Leaving someone exposed to domination would fail that purpose.")
("v287", "item", "v288")
("v286", "value", "v287")
("v252", "item", "v281")
("v289", "type", "Record")
("v289", "entry", "v290")
("v290", "type", "Entry")
("v290", "key", "tag")
("v291", "type", "String")
("v291", "scalar", "p")
("v290", "value", "v291")
("v289", "entry", "v292")
("v292", "type", "Entry")
("v292", "key", "attrs")
("v293", "type", "Record")
("v292", "value", "v293")
("v289", "entry", "v294")
("v294", "type", "Entry")
("v294", "key", "children")
("v295", "type", "Sequence")
("v296", "type", "String")
("v296", "scalar", "That is a theological proposal. It does not follow from a physics equation, a beautiful landscape or a successful computer model. Nor does it explain away cruelty, disaster or the experience of a sincere person who seeks God and finds silence. Those remain difficult questions for this faith to face. ")
("v295", "item", "v296")
