("v351", "value", "v352")
("v349", "value", "v350")
("v346", "entry", "v353")
("v353", "type", "Entry")
("v353", "key", "children")
("v354", "type", "Sequence")
("v355", "type", "String")
("v355", "scalar", "See the scriptural starting points.")
("v354", "item", "v355")
("v353", "value", "v354")
("v344", "item", "v346")
("v343", "value", "v344")
("v317", "item", "v338")
("v356", "type", "Record")
("v356", "entry", "v357")
("v357", "type", "Entry")
("v357", "key", "tag")
("v358", "type", "String")
("v358", "scalar", "p")
("v357", "value", "v358")
("v356", "entry", "v359")
("v359", "type", "Entry")
("v359", "key", "attrs")
("v360", "type", "Record")
("v359", "value", "v360")
("v356", "entry", "v361")
("v361", "type", "Entry")
("v361", "key", "children")
("v362", "type", "Sequence")
("v363", "type", "String")
("v363", "scalar", "Incarnation means God entering embodied human life: dependence, vulnerability, relationships, suffering. The cross brings the question of power into the presence of violence. Resurrection carries the Christian hope that violence and death do not have the final word. I cannot reduce that hope to a metaphor for feeling better, or treat a moving moral story as proof that the resurrection happened.")
("v362", "item", "v363")
("v361", "value", "v362")
("v317", "item", "v356")
("v364", "type", "Record")
("v364", "entry", "v365")
("v365", "type", "Entry")
("v365", "key", "tag")
("v366", "type", "String")
("v366", "scalar", "p")
("v365", "value", "v366")
("v364", "entry", "v367")
("v367", "type", "Entry")
("v367", "key", "attrs")
("v368", "type", "Record")
("v367", "value", "v368")
("v364", "entry", "v369")
("v369", "type", "Entry")
("v369", "key", "children")
("v370", "type", "Sequence")
("v371", "type", "String")
("v371", "scalar", "Self-giving also needs careful handling. Jesus’ service cannot become an instruction for a person with less power to disappear, accept abuse or keep an institution comfortable. The question belongs first to those who hold power: what must I relinquish so someone else can live more freely? A protective boundary can be an act of love.")
("v370", "item", "v371")
("v369", "value", "v370")
("v317", "item", "v364")
("v316", "value", "v317")
