("v401", "type", "Sequence")
("v402", "type", "String")
("v402", "scalar", "How do I read the Bible?")
("v401", "item", "v402")
("v400", "value", "v401")
("v382", "item", "v395")
("v403", "type", "Record")
("v403", "entry", "v404")
("v404", "type", "Entry")
("v404", "key", "tag")
("v405", "type", "String")
("v405", "scalar", "p")
("v404", "value", "v405")
("v403", "entry", "v406")
("v406", "type", "Entry")
("v406", "key", "attrs")
("v407", "type", "Record")
("v406", "value", "v407")
("v403", "entry", "v408")
("v408", "type", "Entry")
("v408", "key", "children")
("v409", "type", "Sequence")
("v410", "type", "String")
("v410", "scalar", "I approach scripture as a collection of writings to be read carefully, in their literary and historical settings, within the larger Christian story. A lament, a proverb, a parable, a law and a letter do different kinds of work. Identifying who is speaking, to whom and in what circumstances comes before turning a sentence into an instruction for today.")
("v409", "item", "v410")
("v408", "value", "v409")
("v382", "item", "v403")
("v411", "type", "Record")
("v411", "entry", "v412")
("v412", "type", "Entry")
("v412", "key", "tag")
("v413", "type", "String")
("v413", "scalar", "p")
("v412", "value", "v413")
("v411", "entry", "v414")
("v414", "type", "Entry")
("v414", "key", "attrs")
("v415", "type", "Record")
("v414", "value", "v415")
("v411", "entry", "v416")
("v416", "type", "Entry")
("v416", "key", "children")
("v417", "type", "Sequence")
("v418", "type", "String")
("v418", "scalar", "Reading through Jesus means taking his account of love of God and neighbour seriously when interpreting the rest. It also requires honesty about the choice I am making. Christians disagree about how scripture, tradition, reason and experience should relate. A Christ-centred reading still has to account for the passages it finds difficult; it cannot quietly remove them. ")
("v417", "item", "v418")
