("v531", "type", "String")
("v531", "scalar", "How do I understand Christianity?")
("v530", "item", "v531")
("v529", "value", "v530")
("v511", "item", "v524")
("v532", "type", "Record")
("v532", "entry", "v533")
("v533", "type", "Entry")
("v533", "key", "tag")
("v534", "type", "String")
("v534", "scalar", "p")
("v533", "value", "v534")
("v532", "entry", "v535")
("v535", "type", "Entry")
("v535", "key", "attrs")
("v536", "type", "Record")
("v535", "value", "v536")
("v532", "entry", "v537")
("v537", "type", "Entry")
("v537", "key", "children")
("v538", "type", "Sequence")
("v539", "type", "String")
("v539", "scalar", "Christianity is a lived, varied tradition of worship, prayer, community, teaching and action, centred on Jesus Christ. A Christian life involves belonging, receiving and practising, as well as making claims about what is true. Its churches and traditions carry gifts and disagreements; their history also includes grave failures.")
("v538", "item", "v539")
("v537", "value", "v538")
("v511", "item", "v532")
("v540", "type", "Record")
("v540", "entry", "v541")
("v541", "type", "Entry")
("v541", "key", "tag")
("v542", "type", "String")
("v542", "scalar", "p")
("v541", "value", "v542")
("v540", "entry", "v543")
("v543", "type", "Entry")
("v543", "key", "attrs")
("v544", "type", "Record")
("v543", "value", "v544")
("v540", "entry", "v545")
("v545", "type", "Entry")
("v545", "key", "children")
("v546", "type", "Sequence")
("v547", "type", "String")
("v547", "scalar", "The corpus develops one kenotic reading within that wider tradition. It draws together self-giving, service, participation and hope. Its own theological audit rejects the claim that this is the uniquely necessary interpretation of Christianity. I should make that limit visible, especially when these ideas inform the software and institutions I build. ")
("v546", "item", "v547")
("v548", "type", "Record")
