("v605", "type", "Sequence")
("v606", "type", "String")
("v606", "scalar", "How do I meet other religions?")
("v605", "item", "v606")
("v604", "value", "v605")
("v586", "item", "v599")
("v607", "type", "Record")
("v607", "entry", "v608")
("v608", "type", "Entry")
("v608", "key", "tag")
("v609", "type", "String")
("v609", "scalar", "p")
("v608", "value", "v609")
("v607", "entry", "v610")
("v610", "type", "Entry")
("v610", "key", "attrs")
("v611", "type", "Record")
("v610", "value", "v611")
("v607", "entry", "v612")
("v612", "type", "Entry")
("v612", "key", "children")
("v613", "type", "Sequence")
("v614", "type", "String")
("v614", "scalar", "I can begin from a Christian commitment and still encounter another tradition with patience and respect. I need to learn what its people actually believe and practise, including disagreements within the tradition. Judaism, Islam, Buddhist and Hindu traditions, other faiths and nonreligious ways of life deserve more than a role in a Christian argument.")
("v613", "item", "v614")
("v612", "value", "v613")
("v586", "item", "v607")
("v615", "type", "Record")
("v615", "entry", "v616")
("v616", "type", "Entry")
("v616", "key", "tag")
("v617", "type", "String")
("v617", "scalar", "p")
("v616", "value", "v617")
("v615", "entry", "v618")
("v618", "type", "Entry")
("v618", "key", "attrs")
("v619", "type", "Record")
("v618", "value", "v619")
("v615", "entry", "v620")
("v620", "type", "Entry")
("v620", "key", "children")
("v621", "type", "Sequence")
("v622", "type", "String")
("v622", "scalar", "I should resist flattening these traditions into interchangeable versions of my own. Their accounts of God, ultimate reality, liberation, salvation and human purpose can differ substantially. Respect allows those differences to remain visible. It also asks me to describe another person’s position in terms they can recognise before I judge it.")
("v621", "item", "v622")
("v620", "value", "v621")
("v586", "item", "v615")
("v623", "type", "Record")
("v623", "entry", "v624")
("v624", "type", "Entry")
("v624", "key", "tag")
("v625", "type", "String")
("v625", "scalar", "p")
("v624", "value", "v625")
("v623", "entry", "v626")
("v626", "type", "Entry")
("v626", "key", "attrs")
("v627", "type", "Record")
("v626", "value", "v627")
("v623", "entry", "v628")
("v628", "type", "Entry")
("v628", "key", "children")
("v629", "type", "Sequence")
("v630", "type", "String")
("v630", "scalar", "Shared compassion, disciplined attention or personal transformation can reveal important human possibilities. They do not automatically settle incompatible religious claims. The corpus makes this point explicitly: similar outcomes can have several explanations. I must apply the same care to a Christian experience as to an experience in another tradition. ")
("v629", "item", "v630")
